<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  STOCKED_POOL_BUILD_1 — the "netted from open water" half of the two-def
  law (spec §0/§2, commission §0): a `fishTypes` entry is an item def
  (`FishBase` lineage), never a race def. These are the generic-fishing-job
  catch representation, distinct from the pawn+meat pair in
  RM_StockedPoolFauna.xml/RM_StockedPoolMeats.xml — a colonist fishing at a
  stocked pool's edge with no husbandry job running can still occasionally
  pull one of these up. Pattern and MayRequire copied from the sibling wild
  table, src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/RUT_WeepingStonesFish_Items.xml
  (RUT_Ikkal etc.) — ParentName="FishBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey".

  🔴 NOT wired into any BiomeDef's `fishTypes` yet — see this mod's About.xml
  and RM_StockedPoolFauna.xml's header for why (RM_WeepingStones BiomeDef
  does not exist; WEEPINGSTONES_RM_MOD_BUILD_1 is still proposed/unclaimed).

  Placeholder art CORRECTION (caught before shipping): the sibling wild
  table's texPaths (AloeVeraA, PincushionPlantA, ...) are NOT vanilla Core
  assets — they are loose PNGs shipped in UtinniPatches' OWN Textures/
  folder (verified: absent from Core's packed textures, present as loose
  files at Mods/UtinniPatches/Textures/Things/Plant/...). Reusing them here
  would make this RM_-tier mod's item art silently depend on RimUtinni
  loading, breaking Q11a's "stand alone" requirement. These items instead
  reuse the real vanilla meat-stack icon (`Things/Item/Resource/MeatFoodRaw/
  Meat_Small`, confirmed directly from `ThingDefGenerator_Meat.cs` via
  RimSage — the engine's own meat-item generator uses exactly this path for
  any race with `baseBodySize < 0.7`, which every one of these eight is),
  tinted per species — genuinely standalone, no cross-mod texture dependency.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="FishBase" MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
    <defName>RM_SkarrinCatch</defName>
    <label>skarrin</label>
    <description>A silver arc netted mid-air at wind-hour — the one catch you make above the water. A missed net is a bite.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Resource/MeatFoodRaw/Meat_Small</texPath>
      <color>(200, 200, 210)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Nutrition>0.10</Nutrition>
      <MarketValue>3</MarketValue>
      <Mass>0.2</Mass>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Rottable">
        <daysToRotStart>2</daysToRotStart>
        <rotDestroys>true</rotDestroys>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

